Hi Caka,

Your data are automatically projected on import and you don't need to worry about it.
When you run akde() the bandwidth is optimized as a part of that calculation. And when the bandwidth is optimized, an autocorrelation model (e.g., OU) needs to be leveraged. Fitting the autocorrelation model is the slowest part of the calculation and is also used for other analyses like occurrence() and speed().
You do want to segment the data into the different behaviors. When the behavior isn't range resident, you can select among non-resident models (e.g., BM and IOU) if you need more parsimony because of limited data, but you cannot calculate AKDEs from those models. You can calculate many other quantities, though, like occurrence() and speed().
Best,
Chris

