Hello,

I am working on an analysis of wintering waterfowl and hoping to characterize habitat associations before range residency is established compared to after range residency is established. Initially I thought I could identify the point on the x-axis of the variogram (time-lag) at which the estimated variogram reaches assymptote (see e.g. pic). Then I would segment the location data at that identified time lag. So for the individual whose variogram is below, I would segement the data 1 day into the sampling period - the first 1 day would be "pre home range establishment/dispersal" locations and the remainder of the dataset would be "home ranging" locations.

Is this an appropriate approach? If not, is there another valid means of segmenting data based upon when range residency is established?

Thanks!

Tori

